    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we need to multiply the numerators together and the denominators together. Let's go through the steps in detail.\n\nStep 1: Identify the numerators and denominators.\nThe first fraction is \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and the second fraction is \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\).\n\nStep 2: Multiply the numerators.\nThe numerator of the product is the product of the numerators of the two fractions:\n\\[1 \\times 3 = 3\\]\n\nStep 3: Multiply the denominators.\nThe denominator of the product is the product of the denominators of the two fractions:\n\\[5 \\times 7 = 35\\]\n\nStep 4: Combine the results.\nThe product of the two fractions is:\n\\[\\frac{3}{35}\\]\n\nSo, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
